Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::a_single_byte_change_always_changes_the_crc`.

The defect: `update` masks each input byte to seven bits before the table lookup, as if the input were ASCII.
Two buffers that differ only in the top bit of one byte then have the same CRC.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_ne!(crc::crc32(&bytes), before)`.

diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs
index c1e8f547e..ca320dfda 100644
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs
@@ -56,3 +56,3 @@ fn update(mut crc: u32, bytes: &[u8]) -> u32 {
     for &b in bytes {
-        crc = TABLE[((crc ^ b as u32) & 0xff) as usize] ^ (crc >> 8);
+        crc = TABLE[((crc ^ (b & 0x7f) as u32) & 0xff) as usize] ^ (crc >> 8);
     }
